WEBVTT

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:06.180
Question 2 would let Rhode Island borrow $120 million for housing and homeownership.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:11.470
A bond is a loan, repaid with interest from the state's general revenues.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:16.830
Each of five bond questions is decided separately, by majority vote.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:23.130
It could pay for new construction, redevelopment, property purchases and infrastructure.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:28.460
At least $25 million would go toward building housing for homeownership.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.420
Up to $10 million could support a program for public housing development.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:44.480
The handbook estimates $72,586,000 in interest, a total cost of $192,586,000.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.730
Those are only estimates, based on 20-year loans at 5 percent interest.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.960
The handbook includes no official argument against the question.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.820
The handbook includes no official argument for the question.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.640
Approve means you support the State issuing these bonds.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.120
Reject means you are against the State issuing these bonds.
